From e9e88dae1eef4e2c19e63c06f12235e662b0ef2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:16:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] glib: Document that XFA script URLs are not checked

poppler_document_xfa_take_urls() hands over whatever URLs the form's
scripts asked for. Say that they may use any scheme and come without user
action, so hosts ask before opening them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 glib/poppler-document.cc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/glib/poppler-document.cc b/glib/poppler-document.cc
index 54ae812..42930f9 100644
--- a/glib/poppler-document.cc
+++ b/glib/poppler-document.cc
@@ -2430,6 +2430,11 @@ gchar **poppler_document_xfa_take_messages(PopplerDocument *document)
  * Returns the URLs the scripts of the XFA form asked to open since the
  * last call, and forgets them.
  *
+ * The URLs come from the document and are not checked: they may use any
+ * scheme, and scripts can request them without any user action. Ask the
+ * user before opening one, as Adobe Reader does, and consider allowing
+ * only web addresses.
+ *
  * Return value: (transfer full) (array zero-terminated=1): the URLs.
  *   Free with g_strfreev().
  *
-- 
